@api @sendgrid @batch @happy @smoke
Feature: SendGrid Mail Batch - Create Batch ID (Happy Path) # features/sendgrid/cancel_scheduled/batch/happy_path.feature:2

  Background:   # features/sendgrid/cancel_scheduled/batch/happy_path.feature:4

  Scenario: POST /v3/mail/batch returns 201 and a valid batch_id           # features/sendgrid/cancel_scheduled/batch/happy_path.feature:10
    Given the API base URL is "https://sendgrid-v3-api.mock.beeceptor.com" # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:29
    When I set request headers                                             # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:158
      | header       | Value    |
      | on-behalf-of | Ut minim |
    When I send a "POST" request to "/v3/mail/batch"                       # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:46
    Then the response status code should be 201                            # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:24
    And the response JSON should not be empty                              # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:312
    And the response JSON should contain keys                              # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:162
      | batch_id |
    And the response JSON path "batch_id" should be a "str"                # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:81

  Scenario: POST /v3/mail/batch returns different batch_id on subsequent calls  # features/sendgrid/cancel_scheduled/batch/happy_path.feature:18
    Given the API base URL is "https://sendgrid-v3-api.mock.beeceptor.com"      # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:29
    When I set request headers                                                  # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:158
      | header       | Value    |
      | on-behalf-of | Ut minim |
    When I send a "POST" request to "/v3/mail/batch"                            # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:46
    Then the response status code should be 201                                 # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:24
    And I store the response JSON path "batch_id" as "batch_id_1"               # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:351
    When I send a "POST" request to "/v3/mail/batch"                            # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:46
    Then the response status code should be 201                                 # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:24
    And I store the response JSON path "batch_id" as "batch_id_2"               # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:351
    Then the stored variables "batch_id_1" and "batch_id_2" should be different # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:371

