@api @sendgrid @scheduled_sends @happy @smoke
Feature: SendGrid Scheduled Sends - Pause/Cancel (Happy Path) # features/sendgrid/cancel_scheduled/scheduled_sends/happy_path.feature:2

  Background:   # features/sendgrid/cancel_scheduled/scheduled_sends/happy_path.feature:4

  Scenario: Pause a scheduled send by batch_id                                                # features/sendgrid/cancel_scheduled/scheduled_sends/happy_path.feature:11
    Given the API base URL is "https://sendgrid-v3-api.mock.beeceptor.com"                    # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:29
    When I set request headers                                                                # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:158
      | header       | Value    |
      | on-behalf-of | Ut minim |
    When I send a "POST" request to "/v3/mail/batch"                                          # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:46
    Then the response status code should be 201                                               # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:24
    And I store the response JSON path "batch_id" as "batch_id"                               # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:351
    When I send a "POST" request to "/v3/user/scheduled_sends" with JSON body using variables # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:242
      """
      {
        "batch_id": "${batch_id}",
        "status": "pause"
      }
      """
    Then the response status code should be 201                                               # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:24
    And the response JSON should contain keys                                                 # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:162
      | batch_id |
      | status   |
      | batch_id |
    And the response JSON path "batch_id" should equal stored variable "batch_id"             # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:398
    And the response JSON path "status" should be "pause"                                     # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:45

  Scenario: Cancel a scheduled send by batch_id                                               # features/sendgrid/cancel_scheduled/scheduled_sends/happy_path.feature:31
    Given the API base URL is "https://sendgrid-v3-api.mock.beeceptor.com"                    # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:29
