      | on-behalf-of | Ut minim |
    When I send a "POST" request to "/v3/mail/batch"                                          # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:46
    Then the response status code should be 201                                               # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:24
    And I store the response JSON path "batch_id" as "batch_id"                               # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:351
    When I send a "POST" request to "/v3/user/scheduled_sends" with JSON body using variables # features/steps/step_http_requests.py:242
      """
      {
        "batch_id": "${batch_id}",
        "status": "cancel"
      }
      """
    Then the response status code should be 201                                               # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:24
    And the response JSON should contain keys                                                 # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:162
      | batch_id |
      | status   |
      | batch_id |
    And the response JSON path "batch_id" should equal stored variable "batch_id"             # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:398
    And the response JSON path "status" should be "cancel"                                    # features/steps/step_http_assertions.py:45

